From 7e425be777ba12acf38f2cae3ad1b51fb378c5a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:21:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Settle an ended local turn's failed lease release
 before admission

Five whys:
1. Automatic Desktop turns showed an ownership card after the previous turn ended.
2. Durable preflight saw the still-present old writer row as another owner.
3. Database release failed and DurableTurnLease cleared the active holder anyway.
4. Preflight had no terminal, process-local custody receipt to retry that exact release.
5. Prior coverage covered lock-abandoned acquisition, not this earlier synthesized gate
   after a non-lock database failure.

Retain an agent-local receipt of failed terminal release, binding process, store,
original session and exact per-turn holder. Preflight retries only that conditional
DELETE and reads ownership again. It never treats a receipt as write authority,
exempts a missing row, steals by PID, repairs corruption or changes marker policy.
Still-failing releases remain coordination-unavailable with lease_self_orphan and
proven holder_pid; holder mismatch is lease_foreign without invented PID/birth.

Historical limitations: retained hub agent.log.10 and agent.log.3 independently
show SQLITE_CORRUPT/append failure, release failure, then automatic SESSION_NOT_OWNED
on two separate occasions. Those logs do not preserve the exact durable
holder or prove process/birth equality. The SQLite fault-injection regression proves
the mechanism on current main, not the identity of either historical writer. Quarantined
handles must still refuse writes; this does not reopen or repair them.

Proof: canonical current-main9fee390a RED: synthesized admission returned None and
emitted SESSION_NOT_OWNED after failed release. Recovery GREEN: 13 focused cases,
including still-failed DB, same-PID foreign holder, custody boundaries, compressed
lineage and racing successor. Existing facade+real CLI takeover tests:17 passed.
Further consumer, mutation, static and independent exact-head CI gates run before ship.

hotspot: tui_gateway/session_lifecycle.py is shared with parent A and sibling C;
this change is limited to durable lease preflight, not marker classification.
